From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:22:56 +0300
Subject: mesa: S3TC DXT1 compression through libspeq on the PS3

The Cell's SPEs (or libspeq's own PPE encoder) compress RGB(A) uploads into DXT1 instead of
Mesa's encoder, so games can use compressed textures (a quarter or an eighth of the VRAM, which
the PS3 also uses as swap) without slow loads. libspeq is loaded at run time: Mesa doesn't
depend on it, and without it, or when it returns an error, Mesa's own encoder runs. All policy
(sizes, which unit, SPEQ_S3TC) lives in libspeq.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/src/mesa/main/texcompress_s3tc.c b/src/mesa/main/texcompress_s3tc.c
--- a/src/mesa/main/texcompress_s3tc.c
+++ b/src/mesa/main/texcompress_s3tc.c
@@ -88,6 +88,10 @@ _mesa_texstore_rgb_dxt1(TEXSTORE_PARAMS)
 
    dst = dstSlices[0];
 
+#if DETECT_ARCH_PPC_64
+   if (!_mesa_s3tc_speq(GL_COMPRESSED_RGB_S3TC_DXT1_EXT, srccomps, pixels, srcWidth,
+                        srcHeight, dst, dstRowStride))
+#endif
    tx_compress_dxt1(srccomps, srcWidth, srcHeight, pixels,
                     dst, dstRowStride, 3);
 
@@ -144,6 +148,10 @@ _mesa_texstore_rgba_dxt1(TEXSTORE_PARAMS)
 
    dst = dstSlices[0];
 
+#if DETECT_ARCH_PPC_64
+   if (!_mesa_s3tc_speq(GL_COMPRESSED_RGBA_S3TC_DXT1_EXT, 4, pixels, srcWidth, srcHeight,
+                        dst, dstRowStride))
+#endif
    tx_compress_dxt1(4, srcWidth, srcHeight, pixels, dst, dstRowStride, 4);
 
    free((void*) tempImage);
